<section class="tab barbs-effect {{#if tab.active}}active{{/if}}" data-group="{{tab.group}}" data-tab="{{tab.id}}">
  <div class="barbs-effect-header">
    <label data-tooltip="Buffs count against Buff Limit and are removed when Downed. Conditions roll Condition Resist when applied from a card.">
      Category <select name="system.category">{{selectOptions categoryChoices selected=barbs.category}}</select>
    </label>
    <label data-tooltip="How many copies can be on one creature. 1 = a new one replaces the old; blank = no limit.">
      Max stacks <input type="number" class="barbs-short" name="flags.barbs.maxStacks" value="{{maxStacks}}" min="1" step="1" placeholder="∞" />
    </label>
    <label class="barbs-check" data-tooltip="Removed after the first roll it modifies, like Assassin's Focus.">
      <input type="checkbox" name="system.singleUse" {{checked barbs.singleUse}} /> Single use
    </label>
    <label class="barbs-check" data-tooltip="Removed when the combat ends (&quot;until the end of combat&quot;), whatever its duration says.">
      <input type="checkbox" name="system.endsWithCombat" {{checked barbs.endsWithCombat}} /> Ends with combat
    </label>
    {{#if grantedBy.length}}
    <span class="barbs-granted-by" data-tooltip="A template: never applies by itself; these effects' triggers copy it onto someone.">
      <i class="fa-solid fa-turn-up fa-rotate-90"></i> Granted by
      {{#each grantedBy as |g|}}<a data-action="openEffect" data-effect-id="{{g.id}}">{{g.name}}</a>{{#unless @last}}, {{/unless}}{{/each}}
    </span>
    {{else}}
    <label class="barbs-check" data-tooltip="Never applies by itself: a trigger on the same item or actor copies it onto someone (&quot;grant Battle Fervor on hit&quot;). Easiest made from a Grant/Inflict trigger's edit button.">
      <input type="checkbox" name="system.template" {{checked barbs.template}} /> Template
    </label>
    {{/if}}
  </div>

  <details class="barbs-section" data-section="bonuses" {{#if open.bonuses}}open{{/if}}>
    <summary>
      <span class="barbs-section-title">Bonuses</span> <span class="barbs-count">{{modifiers.length}}</span>
      <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-question barbs-help-icon" data-tooltip="Pick a bonus from the list (type to search). Character stats (AC, STR, resists, skills...) are always on while the effect is active. Attack bonuses apply to attacks with this weapon if the effect is on a weapon, otherwise to every attack; the other columns narrow them further. Columns that don't apply to a bonus are greyed out."></i>
      <a class="barbs-add" data-action="addModifier" data-tooltip="Add bonus"><i class="fa-solid fa-plus"></i></a>
    </summary>
  <table class="barbs-modifiers barbs-bonuses">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Bonus</th><th>Value</th><th>Damage type</th>
        <th data-tooltip="Only these roll types">Roll</th><th data-tooltip="Only attacks with this kind of weapon">Weapon</th>
        <th data-tooltip="Only when the hit crits">On crit</th><th data-tooltip="Optional conditions, e.g. target:type:demon">Conditions</th>
        <th></th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {{#each modifiers as |m|}}
      <tr data-index="{{m.index}}">
        <td>
          <input type="hidden" name="system.modifiers.{{m.index}}.type" value="{{m.type}}" />
          <input type="hidden" name="system.modifiers.{{m.index}}.key" value="{{m.key}}" />
          <input type="text" class="barbs-bonus-search" placeholder="Search: AC, fire damage, lifesteal..." />
        </td>
        <td><input type="text" name="system.modifiers.{{m.index}}.value" value="{{m.value}}" placeholder="10, 2d8, 20 * @self.buffs" /></td>
        <td><select name="system.modifiers.{{m.index}}.damageType" data-limit="damageType">{{selectOptions @root.damageTypeChoices selected=m.damageType}}</select></td>
        <td><select name="system.modifiers.{{m.index}}.rollType" data-limit="rollType">{{selectOptions @root.rollTypeChoices selected=m.rollType}}</select></td>
        <td><select name="system.modifiers.{{m.index}}.weapon" data-limit="weapon">{{selectOptions @root.weaponChoices selected=m.weapon}}</select></td>
        <td><input type="checkbox" name="system.modifiers.{{m.index}}.onCrit" {{checked m.onCrit}} data-limit="onCrit" /></td>
        <td><input type="text" name="system.modifiers.{{m.index}}.conditions" value="{{m.conditions}}" placeholder="always" data-limit="conditions" /></td>
        <td><a data-action="deleteModifier" data-tooltip="Remove"><i class="fa-solid fa-trash"></i></a></td>
      </tr>
      {{/each}}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  </details>

  {{#unless hideTriggers}}
  <details class="barbs-section" data-section="triggers" {{#if open.triggers}}open{{/if}}>
    <summary>
      <span class="barbs-section-title">Triggers</span> <span class="barbs-count">{{triggers.length}}</span>
      <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-question barbs-help-icon" data-tooltip="When something happens, do something: restore resources, deal damage, grant or inflict a template effect, post a reminder. &quot;Would take damage&quot; triggers change the damage before it lands (reduce it, survive at N health, redirect it, reflect it)."></i>
      <a class="barbs-add" data-action="addTrigger" data-tooltip="Add trigger"><i class="fa-solid fa-plus"></i></a>
    </summary>
    {{#if templateWithTriggers}}
    <p class="notice warning">
      <i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation"></i> This effect is a <strong>Template</strong>, so it's never active and these
      triggers won't run. Put the triggers on a separate, regular effect on the same item, and have them grant this one.
    </p>
    {{/if}}
  <table class="barbs-modifiers barbs-triggers">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>When</th><th>Conditions</th><th data-tooltip="Percent chance; blank = always">%</th><th>Limit</th><th data-tooltip="Remove this effect after it fires">Use up</th><th data-tooltip="A skill check that must succeed, e.g. Armor Mastery: Shields vs @level / 2">Check</th><th>Do</th>
        <th data-tooltip="Amount or text">Value</th><th data-tooltip="Resource (restore) or damage type">Type</th><th>Effect</th>
        <th></th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {{#each triggers as |t|}}
      <tr data-trigger-index="{{t.index}}">
        <td><select name="system.triggers.{{t.index}}.event">{{selectOptions @root.eventChoices selected=t.event}}</select></td>
        <td><input type="text" name="system.triggers.{{t.index}}.conditions" value="{{t.conditions}}" placeholder="always" /></td>
        <td><input type="number" name="system.triggers.{{t.index}}.chance" value="{{#if t.chance}}{{t.chance}}{{/if}}" min="0" max="100" placeholder="—" /></td>
        <td><select name="system.triggers.{{t.index}}.oncePer">{{selectOptions @root.onceChoices selected=t.oncePer}}</select></td>
        <td><input type="checkbox" name="system.triggers.{{t.index}}.consume" {{checked t.consume}} /></td>
        <td><input type="text" name="system.triggers.{{t.index}}.check" value="{{t.check}}" placeholder="Skill vs DC" /></td>
        <td><select name="system.triggers.{{t.index}}.action">{{selectOptions @root.actionChoices selected=t.action}}</select></td>
        <td><input type="text" name="system.triggers.{{t.index}}.value" value="{{t.value}}" placeholder="5, 2d12, text" data-tooltip="Restore/damage: an amount (formula). Reminder: the text. Grant/inflict: leave blank and pick the Effect (or type the template's name here)." /></td>
        <td><input type="text" name="system.triggers.{{t.index}}.type" value="{{t.type}}" placeholder="stamina, lightning" /></td>
        <td class="barbs-trigger-effect">
          {{#if t.inline}}<span class="hint" data-tooltip="Defined by the ability">built in</span>
          {{else}}
          <select name="system.triggers.{{t.index}}.effect">{{selectOptions @root.templateChoices selected=t.effect}}</select>
          <a data-action="editGranted" data-tooltip="Edit the granted effect (makes it if there isn't one yet)"><i class="fa-solid fa-pen-to-square"></i></a>
          {{/if}}
        </td>
        <td><a data-action="deleteTrigger" data-tooltip="Remove"><i class="fa-solid fa-trash"></i></a></td>
      </tr>
      {{/each}}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  </details>
  {{/unless}}

  <details class="barbs-help">
    <summary>Syntax reference: values, conditions, on-hit statuses, triggers</summary>
    <p class="hint">
      <strong>Values</strong> can be formulas: <code>20 * @self.buffs</code>, <code>50 * @target.marks.pursued</code>,
      <code>2d10 * @target.statuses.cursed</code>, <code>@target.health.missingPercent</code>. <code>@self</code>,
      <code>@target</code>, and (for defense bonuses) <code>@attacker</code> have <code>buffs</code>,
      <code>conditions</code>, <code>level</code>, <code>health.percent</code>, and counts like
      <code>statuses.cursed</code>, <code>stacks.&lt;effect&gt;</code>, <code>marks.&lt;effect&gt;</code>. Anything
      reading <code>@target</code> is worked out per target on Apply.
    </p>
    <p class="hint">
      <strong>Conditions</strong>: commas mean "and", <code>|</code> "or", <code>!</code> "not", and numbers compare
      (<code>target:health:percent &lt; 30</code>). Facts: <code>roll:physical</code>, <code>weapon:bow</code>,
      <code>weapon:ranged</code>, <code>ranged</code>/<code>melee</code>, <code>hand:dual</code>,
      <code>ability:tag:spell</code>, <code>ability:class:sniper</code>, <code>area</code>, <code>in-combat</code>;
      <code>self:</code> or <code>target:</code> + <code>type:demon</code>, <code>status:prone</code>,
      <code>effect:rage</code>, <code>health:percent</code>, <code>buffs</code>, <code>level</code>;
      <code>target:mark:&lt;name&gt;</code> (an effect you put on them), <code>target:distance</code>. Defense bonuses
      see <code>attack:…</code>, <code>attacker:…</code>, <code>attacker:distance</code>, and <code>origin:attacker</code>.
    </p>
    <p class="hint">
      <strong>On-hit statuses</strong> take a status id and an optional chance: <code>stunned 25</code> is "25% chance
      to Stun"; damage-over-time ones take an amount, like <code>burned:10 30</code>.
    </p>
    <p class="hint">
      <strong>Triggers</strong>: "you're attacked/hit/damaged" conditions see the attack (<code>attack:…</code>,
      <code>attacker:…</code>, <code>attacker:distance</code>), "you hit"/"you down" see the target. Values can use
      <code>@self</code>, <code>@other</code>, <code>@target</code> or <code>@attacker</code>,
      <code>@hit.damage</code> on hits, and <code>@incoming.damage</code> for "would take damage", whose conditions
      can also use <code>incoming:lethal</code> and <code>attacked</code>. Grant/inflict copy a template effect from the
      same item or actor.
    </p>
  </details>
</section>
